    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Compensated Absences: These amounts represent recovery of costs associated with employee vacation and are being recovered within one year and do not earn a return.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pension: These amounts represent future recoverable pension costs. Amounts are being recovered over the remaining life of the Company's retirement plan.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Smart Meters: Represents amounts associated with the under-recovery of costs associated with the Company's Smart Meter program. Amounts will be collected through the company's next distribution rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">FERC Formula Annual Update Filings: Represents amounts recoverable under the Company's FERC Formula annual update to incorporate actual transmission revenue amount. Amounts are amortized for the period June 1 to May 31.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Tax Adjustment Surcharge (STAS): Represents amounts refundable to customers from the State Tax Adjustment Surcharge. This surcharge pertains to the Company's obligation of state taxes due and any interest and amounts are refunded over a period of one year.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Electric Vehicle Rebate Program: This balance represents spending related to customer rebates for infrastructure to provide electric service to charging stations available to the public. Amounts recoverable were granted in the 2021 rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Solar Purchase Power: These amounts currently represent administrative fees incurred related to the Company's execution of a purchase power agreement (PPA) with a solar facility. Amounts are recoverable from default service customers in accordance with the Company's approved Default Service Plan X.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Eligible Customer Lists 2024: Represents the costs incurred by the Company in order to update the electric Eligible Customers Lists (ECL), which are made available to Electric Generation Suppliers (EGSs). Costs will be recovered over a period of up to three years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">RFP Generation: Represents the over collection of amounts related to supplier auctions of small and medium commercial and industrial generation customers. Amounts are refunded over a period of two years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">POLR X: These amounts represent recoverable costs incurred related to the POLR X filing and are amortized over a period of up to four years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Rate Case Distribution 2024: These amounts represent recoverable costs incurred related to the Company's distribution rate case filing.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Annual Transmission Service Change Filing: These amounts represent the true up of costs under the PUC Transmission Service Charge annual filing which are amortized June thru May each year.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Grant Writing: These amounts represent represent costs incurred to prepare, apply, administer, and otherwise execute on opportunities for federal funding made available by the IIJA.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">DSIC: This balance relates to an undercollection of DSIC revenue. Amounts are recoverable consistent with the Company's tariff.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">OPEB Cost: These amounts represent future recoverable other post employment benefit (OPEB) costs. Amounts are determined and recovered based on the Company's actuarial calculations and established rates.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">RME Market Enhancement: The Retail Market Enhancement Surcharge (RMES) is a cost recovery mechanism to recover all eligible costs associated with implementing Commission-mandated activities, programs, projects, services etc. to enhance the competitive energy market in Pennsylvania.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Legacy Liability: Amount relates to formerly owned generation plants and operations, mainly ash disposal sites where the Company has obtained rate recovery of certain environmental costs, but has not paid out all its obligations, thus requiring a regulatory liability.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">RFP Generation: Represents the over collection of amounts related to supplier auctions of small and medium commercial and industrial generation customers. Amounts are refunded over a period of two years</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Regulatory Tax Liability: Represents a net regulatory liability on regulated utility property that includes the excess deferred income tax flow back to customers over the average remaining book life of the regulated property resulting from the corporate tax rate reduction; net of the FAS 109 property basis differences and corresponding FAS 109 tax gross up resulting from book depreciation versus accelerated tax deduction that are being recovered over the remaining depreciable life of the regulated utility property, plant and equipment.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Act 129 Energy Efficiency: Represents refundable amounts from customers for the Company's Energy Efficiency Surcharge. Amounts will be will be refunded/recouped consistent with the Company's tariff.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Electric Vehicle Registration Credits: This balance represents the underspend related to the electric vehicle customer registration credits allowed annually via the Company's approved rate case settlements and are recovered over a period of three years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pension Rate Case Settlement: Represents amounts recorded as a regulatory liability related to pension cost items.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">State Tax Adjustment Surcharge (STAS): Represents amounts refundable to customers from the State Tax Adjustment Surcharge. This surcharge pertains to the Company's obligation of state taxes due and any interest and amounts are refunded over a period of one year.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">FERC Formula Annual Update Filing: Represents amounts refundable under the Company's FERC Formula annual update to incorporate actual transmission revenue amount. Amounts are amortized for the period June 1 to May 31.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Annual Transmission Surcharge: Represents amounts recoverable from customers related to the PUC Transmission Service Charge Surcharge. Amounts are recovered over a period of two years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Rider 5 Surcharge: A cost recovery mechanism for the Universal Service and Energy Conservation plan which encompasses the policies, practices and services that enables eligible customers to maintain utility service.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
